meta {
  name: Models
  seq: 11
}

docs {
  Managing the AI models: the catalog and its routes, what each backend model
  costs, the operator's own endpoints, retirement, and the read-only views.

  Reading needs `models.view` (every role). Changing the catalog, routes,
  endpoints and retirement needs `models.manage` (owner, operator). Prices need
  `models.prices` (owner, finance). Every change takes a `reason`; changes to an
  internal model (the workflow builder, the personal assistant), and anything
  that stores a secret, also take a fresh `totp_code`.

  Start with `Health`: it lists everything wrong (a model with no price, a
  route nobody can run, a retirement with no replacement). The same report is
  `php artisan model-catalog:doctor`.

  List requests store the first row's id (`saModelId`, `saRouteId`,
  `saPriceId`, `saEndpointId`) so the rest of the folder works.
}
